        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: लक्षणम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लक्षणम् — lakṣaṇam — \"a sign of something to come; a mark\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि ज्वरस्य लक्षणम् अस्ति, तर्हि वैद्यं पश्यतु। yadi jvarasya lakṣaṇam asti, tarhi vaidyaṃ paśyatu. If there is a sign of fever, see a doctor."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लक्षणम् (lakṣaṇam) comes from the root √lakṣ, \"to mark, to perceive\"; MW gives lakṣaṇa \"a mark, a sign, a symbol, a token, a characteristic\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
